course: dictionary
lesson: 2510
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find the right one. «Decent» can mean good enough, kind and fair, polite, or dressed.
explain: «Poor old Ratty — a decent fellow, but not clever.» The word «but» is a clue. It tells you that decent is praise for being good and kind, not for being clever. A decent person is honest, kind and fair to others.
explain: «...only at a decent speed on a smooth road» does not mean very fast. It means a speed that is good enough and sensible. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Decent means good enough, of an acceptable or fairly good quality.
fact: A decent person is honest, kind and fair to others.
fact: Decent can also mean polite and respectable, following what people think is proper.
fact: «Are you decent?» means «Are you dressed?», so someone knows they can come in.
fact: In UK and Australian slang, «decent» can mean really good.
exercise: «Poor old Ratty — a decent fellow, but not clever.» What does decent mean here? | *Kind and fair | Lost in the woods | Very fast | Dressed in smart clothes
exercise: «Riding no-hands only works at a decent speed on a smooth road.» What does decent speed mean? | A speed that is very fast | A speed that is too slow to move | *A fair, sensible speed that is good enough | A speed for a race
exercise: Mum calls through the bathroom door, «Are you decent?» What does she mean? | Are you lost? | Are you finished with your bath? | *Are you dressed? | Are you hungry?
test: The barge-woman says he would pass for «quite a decent-looking Toad!» What does decent-looking mean? | Hidden from view | Very dirty | Shouting loudly | *Quite good-looking
test: Tom ate «a decent amount» of cake. What does decent amount mean? | *A fair, good-enough amount | A huge pile that made him sick | A tiny crumb | None at all
exam: In «It was decent of you to share your sweets», what does decent mean? | *Kind and fair | Very sweet, like sugar | Rude and loud | Late for school
